    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "thanks. can you explain more about the center of gravity part? like if we use those patterns, how do we make sure the load doesn't shift mid-stack or get knocked out of alignment while we're lifting it into the higher racks? we've had some close calls.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "In pallet stacking, the center of gravity is the point at which the weight shifts. To minimize this shift, group heavy items weighing closest to the center, using the same corner and 'inned' positions for each stack. Also, keep a leveler or pad between pallets to ensure smooth transitions and application of even pressure while storing lifted items. By doing so, the center of gravity remains balanced, ensuring structural stability.",
      "source": "target",
